WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.478
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:16.296
Unit twenty-one: Will (predictions, offers, promises). Today you will make predictions, offers and promises.

4
00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.237
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.688
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.284
Will.

7
00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:29.618
Will means used for future predictions, offers and promises.

8
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:31.624
It will rain tomorrow.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:34.869
Your turn. Say: Will.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.746
Will.

11
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:40.159
Won't.

12
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.662
Won't means will not.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.390
I won't be late.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:47.206
Your turn. Say: Won't.

15
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:50.928
Won't.

16
00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:52.568
Predict.

17
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:55.594
Predict means to say what will happen.

18
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.974
I predict that it will rain.

19
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:01.027
Your turn. Say: Predict.

20
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:04.647
Predict.

21
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:06.292
Offer.

22
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:09.887
Offer means to say that you will give or do something.

23
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:11.798
I will help you.

24
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.873
Your turn. Say: Offer.

25
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:18.491
Offer.

26
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.205
Promise.

27
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:24.180
Promise means to say that you will definitely do something.

28
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:26.202
I promise to call.

29
00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:29.039
Your turn. Say: Promise.

30
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:32.878
Promise.

31
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:34.502
Future.

32
00:01:35.517 --> 00:01:37.714
Future means the time that will come.

33
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.177
In the future, we will fly.

34
00:01:40.783 --> 00:01:43.006
Your turn. Say: Future.

35
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:46.682
Future.

36
00:01:47.417 --> 00:01:48.348
Probably.

37
00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.199
Probably means very likely.

38
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:53.295
It will probably rain.

39
00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:56.512
Your turn. Say: Probably.

40
00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:00.484
Probably.

41
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:01.891
I'll.

42
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:04.163
I'll means I will.

43
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:05.798
I'll help you.

44
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:08.676
Your turn. Say: I'll.

45
00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:12.337
I'll.

46
00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:16.865
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.717 --> 00:02:21.217
Visal, I have a heavy bag. What can you say to help me?

48
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:31.220
I'll help you. We use will for offers and decisions made at the moment of speaking. I will carry it. The short form is I'll.

49
00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:34.374
What about predictions and promises?

50
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:49.301
Predictions: It will rain tomorrow. People will live on Mars. Promises: I will call you. I won't be late. With probably, the word goes after will: It will probably rain.

51
00:02:50.417 --> 00:02:52.637
How do we make negatives and questions?

52
00:02:53.750 --> 00:03:07.672
Will not or won't: I won't tell anyone. Questions: Will you help me? Yes, I will. No, I won't. After will we always use the base verb: She will come, not she will comes.

53
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:10.334
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:13.543
Grammar focus: Will plus base verb.

55
00:03:13.843 --> 00:03:15.041
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.494
I will help you with your bag.

57
00:03:18.383 --> 00:03:20.151
It will probably rain tomorrow.

58
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.446
I won't be late again.

59
00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:30.757
Use will + base verb for predictions, offers, promises and quick decisions. Negative: won't. Probably goes after will.

60
00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:34.796
Be careful! Don't say: She will comes tomorrow.

61
00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:38.942
Say: She will come tomorrow.

62
00:03:39.242 --> 00:03:41.160
Use the base verb after will.

63
00:03:41.967 --> 00:03:45.211
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.197
Offers, Promises and Predictions.

65
00:03:48.497 --> 00:03:51.498
I'll carry your bag. It looks very heavy.

66
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.732
I promise that I won't be late tomorrow.

67
00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:57.640
It will probably rain this evening.

68
00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:01.655
In the future, people will drive electric cars.

69
00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.110
Will you help me? Yes, I will.

70
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.434
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.866
It looks heavy. I blank help you.

72
00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:17.285
A, will. B, am going. C, do.

73
00:04:20.833 --> 00:04:22.392
The answer is A: will.

74
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.052
Look at the clouds. It blank rain. (prediction)

75
00:04:27.352 --> 00:04:30.600
A, will. B, was. C, is rain.

76
00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.075
The answer is A: will.

77
00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:39.274
I promise I blank tell anyone.

78
00:04:39.574 --> 00:04:42.519
A, will. B, won't. C, didn't.

79
00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.846
The answer is B: won't.

80
00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:50.704
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:51.004 --> 00:04:56.898
A, She will comes tomorrow.. B, She will come tomorrow.. C, She will to come tomorrow..

82
00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.920
The answer is B: She will come tomorrow..

83
00:05:04.083 --> 00:05:07.464
According to the reading, what will people drive in the future?

84
00:05:07.764 --> 00:05:11.801
A, electric cars. B, bikes. C, buses.

85
00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.610
The answer is A: electric cars.

86
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.824
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:22.683 --> 00:05:25.263
Make one prediction and one promise with 'will'.

88
00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.457
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:35.757 --> 00:05:47.273
I think it will rain tomorrow, so we will need umbrellas. I promise that I will help you with your homework. I use will for predictions and promises. After will, I use the base verb.

90
00:05:47.573 --> 00:05:49.329
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.217 --> 00:05:54.703
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and will plus base verb.

92
00:05:55.003 --> 00:06:00.976
Today's value is trust-building. Earn trust slowly, through honest words and kept promises.

93
00:06:01.276 --> 00:06:04.091
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.391 --> 00:06:06.672
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

